\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Determine a fully specified asymptotic equivalent for
\[
V(x)=\#\{m\leq x:m=\phi(n)\text{ for some positive integer }n\},
\]
counting each distinct totient value once.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Determine a fully specified asymptotic equivalent for the number $V(x)=\#\{m\leq x:m=\phi(n)\text{ for some positive integer }n\}$ of distinct totient values at most $x$, counting each value once.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=List_of_unsolved_problems_in_mathematics&oldid=1366636767#Number_theory}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-asymptotic-formula-for-the-number-of-totients-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

