\section*{An explicit asymptotic formula for the number of totients}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 024; 2026-09-25), the asserted result is that distinct totient values admit an explicit asymptotic with a coefficient obtained from finite arithmetic approximations, and the count is regularly varying with index one.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 024; 2026-09-25), long prime prefixes and smooth cofactors cover almost all values. A collision estimate identifies when different shortened tuples represent the same totient, and a sieve comparison determines the main term after those collisions are removed.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 024; 2026-09-25).

\subsection{Formal verification}
For manuscript 1 (family 024; 2026-09-25), OpenAI lists Lean statements for this assertion: distinct totient values admit an explicit asymptotic with a coefficient obtained from finite arithmetic approximations, and the count is regularly varying with index one.

The central assertion is within the documented formal scope; the additional applications retain their own scope limits.

The linked family Comparator checks are \texttt{TotientAsymptotic.lean}, \texttt{TotientCompanionZero.lean}.

Their named declarations include \texttt{OAI.TotientAsymptotic.coefficient\_nonnegative}, \texttt{OAI.TotientAsymptotic.companion\_zero\_case}, \texttt{OAI.TotientAsymptotic.totient\_asymptotic\_formula}, \texttt{OAI.TotientAsymptotic.weighted\_totient\_asymptotic}, \texttt{OAI.TotientAsymptotic.weighted\_totient\_one\_two}.

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

